<h1 id="cast">CAST</h1>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Cast</code> is also called currying; it’s simply a type conversion process. In iOS we often force-cast some data type. Every time we have to write some bloated code, so people get used to writing macros to check whether an instance variable belongs to a certain class.</p>

<p>Below I’ll share some commonly used macros that leverage the dynamic features provided by the Objective-C runtime to handle common type checks.</p>

